  Prefab: {fileID: 6625514644646704096, guid: 1f6a6789373206e498f996cb54aeedb1, type: 3}
  Interactable: {fileID: 5048261325816738630, guid: 1f6a6789373206e498f996cb54aeedb1, type: 3}
  TextFields:
  - Dear Astrid,
  - "I got your letter, Bear. I understand why the auroras make you nervous. Ever
    since the CME, people don\u2019t trust the sky. There are rumors, stories, superstitions.
    Some folks won\u2019t even go out at night. \n\nThe truth is, coronal mass ejections
    happen all the time. They aren't usually a problem. Two years ago, when the alert
    went out, countries around the world shut down the power grid to protect it.
    No big deal\u2014just protocol.\n\nThen the second wave hit. Stronger, faster,
    and it struck just as systems were coming back online. Total overload. A rare
    one-two punch from the sun. Thankfully, we've learned from this. We'll be better
    prepared if it ever happens again. \n\nWe've always looked for meaning in the
    stars... so I guess it makes sense that people feel like the night sky betrayed
    them. But when we don't have the night sky, we\u2019re missing out on part of
    our history. Our shared humanity. That\u2019s probably one of the few things
    Elijah and I agree on. \n\nAnyhow. If you see the Northern Lights again, just
    enjoy them. They\u2019re really something, huh?"
  - Love,<br>Dad
